<title>COLOMBIA: Foreign investment in Colombian stocks rises.</title>
<headline>Foreign investment in Colombian stocks rises.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign investment funds had a total of about $1.16 billion riding on the Colombian stock market at the end of May, a 26.2 percent increase over the same month last year, figures from the Securities Superintendency showed.</p>
<p>The preliminary figures represented a 0.51 percent increase over April.</p>
<p>Investment in preferred Colombian shares or ADRs issued abroad was up 1.04 percent in the May-to-May period to a total of $483 million, the superintendency said.</p>
<p>((-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
